"comparison": "Both JPM and Citi explicitly include Credit Valuation Adjustment (CVA) and associated CVA hedges in their Credit Portfolio VaR. JPM states that its VaR 'includes the derivative CVA, hedges of the CVA... and credit protection purchased against certain retained loans', while Citi's credit portfolio is 'composed of... the CVA relating to derivative counterparties, all associated CVA hedges'. A key difference is that Citi explicitly excludes FVA and DVA from this component, whereas JPM's disclosure focuses on the inclusion of CVA and credit protection, noting that CVA components for specific counterparties were removed due to widened spreads.",
